{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/798189-the-problem-with-bunks","id":798189,"title":"The problem with Bunks...","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Changeling: The Dreaming"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-01-02T03:49:01-08:00","id":798189,"title":"The problem with Bunks...","content":"Okay, so this issue has been mentioned a few times over at the KS, but I'm raising it here as this seems a better place for discussions.<br /> <br /> I like the idea behind Bunks but I rarely think they've been well executed. I like the idea in the teaser that they should include risk, materials and/or time. I'm kinda okay with them requiring attention too, but I feel like this attention should be that of the Dreaming, and not of the public/media/police, however. A big part of changeling is the secrecy and hidden-in-plain-sight thing.<br /> <br /> What I don't like are the examples of Bunks often given in the text. These are variously silly, childish or desperately hip (photobombing a selfie?) and only occasionally thematically appropriate. For me, Bunks should be more akin to Mage's instruments, but drawing from a fairytale/mythological/folkloric paradigm. Draw a door in chalk for Portal Passage. Cover yourself in dirt for Hidden Form. Read the Tarot for Omen. You should always have the option of doing a level one Bunk in the same turn as the casting, too, or everyone will just Unleash all the time.<br /> <br /> Now, that could still leave room for the fishmalk stuff if you want to do that, but the system itself wouldn't outright call for you to pull down your pants and flick V-signs between your legs at your friendly neighbourhood Garou. <br /> <br /> I think I also liked the elegance of the old rating system, where you simply deduct the Bunk level from the difficulty. The new modifiers seem less intuitive to me, but perhaps that's because this is just a teaser. <br /> <br /> I'd like more examples of Bunks that are drawn from lore about fae.<br /> <br /> What do others think?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-02T04:17:20-08:00","id":798195,"title":"","content":"Well, actually bunks are not about weaving the glamour, at least not in 2nd edition. Bunks are about making the magic much more normal to mundane eyes. Nobody excepts you to be fast after claping your hands or after doing &quot;nothing&quot;. However, if you are becoming faster and faster while dancing it will be much more &quot;normal&quot;. Bunks are tools to breach mists just like glamour.<br /> <br /> Cantrips were not &quot;a way to weave glamour&quot;. They were the arts of dreaming, you dream and make things happen, thats why you are fae. Now, with new edition everything changed. Bunks are not a way to clear mists from mundane eyes, they are ways to open a door. Bunks should not affect the dreaming, but they should affect the eyes of the banal.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7562-kokorowatari","name":"KokoroWatari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7562_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"58"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-02T05:12:49-08:00","id":798209,"title":"","content":"Bunks are a creative act through which glamour is focused. They can be anything, limited only by a player's imagination. They can range from the extremely silly, like mooning someone to hopscotch them away from you, to the serious, like punching someone in the face to cast holly strike on them.<br /> <br /> To use an example I saw from someone on the Kickstarter recently, if pulling down a cop's pants to cast veiled eyes on yourself seems stupid and out of character, don't do it. Instead, put on some camouflage face paint, or dramatically dive behind cover to hide, or throw a smoke bomb with which to vanish. Your bunk is up to you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Charlie Cantrell</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer <hr />Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition, Conquering Heroes, Book of Freeholds, Guide to the Night, C20 Players Guide","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","name":"PookaKnight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"690"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-02T05:27:54-08:00","id":798211,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure I buy that interpretation. All the fluff points to Bunks as a way of soliciting the Dreaming to weave your Glamour, rather than making magic more mundane or acceptable to mortal eyes.<br /> <br /> p.8: 'Bunk: The price Glamour exacts for its power.'<br /> <br /> The description on p.205 runs with this definition.<br /> <br /> Bunks are specifically ways to coax Glamour. The Unleashing section in C20 also talks about coaxing Glamour. It's still central to the system.<br /> <br /> Bunks are also performed even if there are no witnesses. They've never been for the benefit of mortals, but for the Dreaming. Now, if that's changed in C20, and that ties into a wider change of focus (that of balance between Banality and Glamour, which has always been present in the game but very inconsistently) it might work. But I don't think the example Bunks given seem particularly good at illustrating that point either. <br /> <br /> Getting on the front page of a newspaper appears to have nothing to do with magic if taken at face value. Maybe drawing attention to magic in such a way that you make the front cover of a newspaper would be a powerful act, but it's not something you can guarantee in the moment. That seems more like the kind of condition which would give you a boost of temporary Glamour for bringing magic into the world (sort of like the Legend Background), rather than a Bunk. The Bunk would surely be the action which eventually led to that news coverage? The descriptions of Bunks should specify that initial action and not the later consequence, because otherwise it's not a helpful illustration. C20 should make the system clearer and not more muddled.<br /> <br /> But I still feel strongly that any Bunk should resonate with the desired effect of a cantrip. It should feel appropriate rather than being merely widely seen.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-02T05:36:30-08:00","id":798214,"title":"","content":"Sorry, our posts crossed!<br /> <br /> PookaKnight, while that's true, the text we've been presented with doesn't give us those examples. Instead it gives the seemingly unmagical examples instead.<br /> <br /> C20 needs to make the game more specific and fill in the gaps. I don't want to have to infer or house rule even more stuff. It should be clear. Give us some examples of a wide range of Bunks, or the text isn't doing its job. From that section alone, the emphasis still seems to be on the daft stuff, but now it feels even less relevant.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-02T06:49:21-08:00","id":798231,"title":"","content":"Well, there is an thing called as consensus, even fae has banality. I think they were much more dream creature before. They are fae now. However, magic system become much more mage-like.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7562-kokorowatari","name":"KokoroWatari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7562_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"58"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-02T07:44:29-08:00","id":798248,"title":"","content":"Consensus is a thing in Mage: The Ascension, but it's a meaningless term as a game mechanic in Changeling: The Dreaming.<br /> <br /> The Tuatha and their children fostered the rise of humanity and their higher emotions, and together they reshaped the Earth and the Dreaming into a form more hospitable to humans and fae alike. The fae forgot how interconnected humans and the Dreaming are and got so wrapped up in their own petty conflicts that they broke the world giving rise to banality and apathy. Now the worlds hang by a single thread, and only changelings working together with humanity have any chance of restoring it. The odds are stacked against them. The fae are dying and have lost touch of all but the tiniest embers of their power. Humanity has lost what makes them great, preferring rote and safety to building anything grand. Standing outside it all are displaced primordial nightmares sabotaging the efforts of the fae and humanity while waiting for their chance to reclaim what once was theirs.<br /> <br /> Against this backdrop, self important will workers are just a bunch of clueless mortals who have managed to tap into an ancient power they don't even begin to understand.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Charlie Cantrell</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer <hr />Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition, Conquering Heroes, Book of Freeholds, Guide to the Night, C20 Players Guide","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","name":"PookaKnight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"690"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-02T08:00:01-08:00","id":798257,"title":"","content":"I think seriousness/silliness should be considered separately for the character. What works for a more outlandish pooka or knocker will not be what works for a troll or sidhe lord.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1136-wolfgar","name":"Wolfgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"646"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-02T08:47:40-08:00","id":798277,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wolfgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/798189-the-problem-with-bunks?p=798257#post798257\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think seriousness/silliness should be considered separately for the character. What works for a more outlandish pooka or knocker will not be what works for a troll or sidhe lord.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well exactly. But the ones given in the C20 teaser include photobombing a selfie and streaking through a sports stadium. These seem rather detached from context and paradigm (to steal a Mage term).<br /> <br /> Will we be seeing examples of Bunks that make sense for the individual changeling using them? Or will the text continue to promote the image of them as childish things you do to get a difficulty modifier? I'm worried because the latter is the kind of thing that lots of people have complained about regarding the often inconsistent tone of the game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-02T09:13:16-08:00","id":798285,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PookaKnight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/798189-the-problem-with-bunks?p=798248#post798248\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Consensus is a thing in Mage: The Ascension, but it's a meaningless term as a game mechanic in Changeling: The Dreaming.</div> </div> </div> </div>Isn't consensus mean banality? If everybody agree on something and classify it (projecting it to high umbra) makes it banal?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7562-kokorowatari","name":"KokoroWatari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7562_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"58"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-02T09:19:50-08:00","id":798288,"title":"","content":"Just because people agree on a system of classification, doesn't mean it's banal. If it were, the kiths themselves would be a form of banality.<br /> <br /> Banality is an absence of wonder, going through the motions without thinking about what you're doing, surrendering to the status quo because that's just the way things are, following the crowd because conformity in and of itself is the end goal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Charlie Cantrell</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer <hr />Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition, Conquering Heroes, Book of Freeholds, Guide to the Night, C20 Players Guide","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","name":"PookaKnight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"690"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-02T09:28:22-08:00","id":798293,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PookaKnight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/798189-the-problem-with-bunks?p=798288#post798288\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just because people agree on a system of classification, doesn't mean it's banal. If it were, the kiths themselves would be a form of banality.<br /> <br /> Banality is an absence of wonder, going through the motions without thinking about what you're doing, surrendering to the status quo because that's just the way things are, following the crowd because conformity in and of itself is the end goal.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree with that, but it does not change that consensus plays a huge role in it. Mists are clouding our minds because people does not believe in fae, and this is part of &quot;consensus&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7562-kokorowatari","name":"KokoroWatari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7562_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"58"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-02T09:42:09-08:00","id":798296,"title":"","content":"Consensus doesn't define reality in Changeling, that's a Mage thing. The mundane and the chimerical are both real. The mists are a defense mechanism of the Dreaming to hide from banality. The Dreaming continues to exist even though very few humans believe in it. Getting humanity to be less banal will certainly help things, but it won't fix everything.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Charlie Cantrell</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer <hr />Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition, Conquering Heroes, Book of Freeholds, Guide to the Night, C20 Players Guide","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","name":"PookaKnight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"690"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-02T17:49:18-08:00","id":798512,"title":"","content":"Bunks are the opposite of what Kokoro seems to think. They are not about making the magical mundane but about cracking the edges of mundanity and making it magical. The masquerade/paradox etc of the the Fae is the mists and Banality, people soon forget and make excuses the fae don't need to hide on theirown or act hidden","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-03T03:44:28-08:00","id":799367,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/798189-the-problem-with-bunks?p=798512#post798512\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Bunks are the opposite of what Kokoro seems to think. They are not about making the magical mundane but about cracking the edges of mundanity and making it magical.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, actually I am not indicating that bunks are making magic more mundane. Oppositely, it lowers the mundane eyes banality. Making casted magic more possible to mundane eye.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7562-kokorowatari","name":"KokoroWatari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7562_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"58"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-03T05:09:05-08:00","id":799535,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KokoroWatari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/798189-the-problem-with-bunks?p=799367#post799367\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, actually I am not indicating that bunks are making magic more mundane. Oppositely, it lowers the mundane eyes banality. Making casted magic more possible to mundane eye.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes and no. Cantrips in the old system had to overcome the target's Banality, thus making mundane eyes see the magical. But Bunks themselves are more to do with the relationship between a changeling and the Dreaming than between a changeling and her target.<br /> <br /> Re-reading this, it looks like I hate Bunks, and I don't. I'll clarify: I love Bunks, I just think they're part of the problem with tone that Changeling sometimes had, and so they're a key part of what will fix that. <br /> <br /> I'm looking forward to a more concrete system for creating Bunks (I mean, what's the difference between each level of Bunk? Second Edition didn't give concrete rules for this). I want to be able to clearly say, 'This is a level one Bunk. This is a level four Bunk.'<br /> <br /> I'm also hoping for Bunks that feel more 'fae' and less 'make believe'/'playground'. The latter is fine for some childlings, but it doesn't seem to fit with the folklore much.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-03T10:07:31-08:00","id":799682,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KokoroWatari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/798189-the-problem-with-bunks?p=799367#post799367\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, actually I am not indicating that bunks are making magic more mundane. Oppositely, it lowers the mundane eyes banality. Making casted magic more possible to mundane eye.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I think of it more like smashing a window into mundanity. Briefly imposing vs making thing smooth out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-04T11:31:30-08:00","id":800662,"title":"","content":"In practice, what <i>should</i> the difference between a Bunk performed by a Changeling and a Practice (i.e. the actual &quot;thing&quot; being done for a given spell) performed by a Mage be?<br /> <br /> If a Changeling is reading the Tarot to perform Omen, and a Mage is reading the Tarot for a Time/Entropy future-prediction/manipulation effect, is this &quot;as it should be,&quot; or is this a rare instance where a Bunk and a Practice are the same thing? Should a Changeling's Bunks feel and/or be different if written about by an in-game observer who only sees what the funny people are doing with his mundane eyes?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/827-segev","name":"Segev","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1001"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-04T13:27:49-08:00","id":800707,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Segev</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/798189-the-problem-with-bunks?p=800662#post800662\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In practice, what <i>should</i> the difference between a Bunk performed by a Changeling and a Practice (i.e. the actual &quot;thing&quot; being done for a given spell) performed by a Mage be?<br /> <br /> If a Changeling is reading the Tarot to perform Omen, and a Mage is reading the Tarot for a Time/Entropy future-prediction/manipulation effect, is this &quot;as it should be,&quot; or is this a rare instance where a Bunk and a Practice are the same thing? Should a Changeling's Bunks feel and/or be different if written about by an in-game observer who only sees what the funny people are doing with his mundane eyes?</div> </div> </div> </div>Cosmetically? They might be similar, they might be different. It really depends on how the player/ST describes what they're doing. I've been to a few tarot readers for fun in my time; not one of them has read the cards the same way as any other. Some readers chant over their cards. Others flip them in silence. Some have incense, others smoke cigarettes. There are dozens of types of decks, dozens of types of layouts, dozens of ways to shuffle and cut a deck, and even card interpretations are different and randomized. If a mage and a changeling are sitting side by side using their magic to read the future with tarot cards, that (in my opinion) is probably going to be where the similarity begins and ends. <br /> <br /> As for the &quot;feeling&quot;: they're completely different systems from completely different sources of power. A changeling is not a mage, and a mage is not a changeling. They don't use the same magic. Magical similarities should be superficial at best, imo.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Luka Carroll</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer &amp; Developer<br /> <i>Working On: </i>C20 Player's Guide, Lunars<br /> <i>Worked On: </i>V20 TMR, Demon STG, C20, Book of Freeholds, Conquering Heroes, Building A Legend, Dragon-Blooded, The Realm","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3785-luka-c","name":"Luka C","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3785_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"175"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-04T14:21:01-08:00","id":800737,"title":"","content":"While a valid answer to my question, I think you missed the point of it. This is probably my fault.<br /> <br /> Let's say that a Changeling wants to use a Cantrip, and a Mage wants to use a magical effect that has a similar (if not identical) result. Maybe both are trying to jump over a fence, one with Hopscotch and the other with either a Life or Forces effect.<br /> <br /> Is there anything the Changeling should or could do as a Bunk that the Mage should or could not do as his Practice? Is there anything the Mage should or could do as his Practice that the Changeling should or could not do as his Bunk?<br /> <br /> Could a mortal scholar, who is unable to see magic in any special way, tell the difference based solely on witnessing a Bunk and a Practice between the two?<br /> <br /> <br /> What I'm getting at is a question of whether &quot;ideas for the stunt&quot; should be different depending on whether it's a Bunk or a Practice, and if so, how. That is, if you made a list of ideas for Bunks for particular effects, and a list of ideas for Practices for different effects, would those lists be different? If so, why and how?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/827-segev","name":"Segev","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1001"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-04T17:52:22-08:00","id":800851,"title":"","content":"There are various differences between Bunks and Practices.<br /> <br /> One difference was mentioned. They serve to pull different &quot;magical strings&quot;, so to speak. Practices are to Focus the Will into an instrument in order to alter reality, while Bunks are there to ease the channeling of Glamour into a Banality laden world.<br /> <br /> Other difference, more important to me, it's what they mean for the users.<br /> <br /> As their name implies, Practices are more than a convenient way of casting. Practices are something that the Mage has to, well, practice. They're a discipline used to do magick and, many times, a way of living. <br /> Mages believe that their focused Practice it's the cause of the alteration of Reality. Even after they leave their Instruments, Mages still believe in their Practices, and old Instruments are still capable of giving a Bonus.<br /> <br /> Changelings, in contrast, use Bunks for convenience and flair. They don't believe that Bunks have the power, or that certain Bunks, used in certain ways, are a better way of releasing magic than others. To faes, Bunks are a way to ease the usage of magic, not a path to have acces to it. <br /> <br /> If a certain Bunk seems appropiate for the scene and the fae, they have no problem on doing it. For a mage that would be unthinkable, you can't switch to a different Practice in the moment to do something that &quot;seems glamorous&quot;.<br /> In the same sense, faes would find ridiculous to defend a particular kind of Bunks over others, and fight over wich Bunk it's better for the world <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> The outside observer wouldn't be able to notice the difference if she hasn't supernatural means to do it, but the practitioners would do them with a very different intent <br /> \u200b<br /> But, more to the point, while a certain type of Bunks could be identical in its appearance to certain Practices, this can't always be the case. Glamour springs from histories and dreams and Practices spring from visionary ideas about how the world works, and many are tried and true ways to reach magic in human folklore.<br /> Both can overlap a lot. However some Practices might be Banal, tied to Banal ways of understanding the world, and thus unappropiate to Changelings. Even if Weid Sciece it's &quot;practiced&quot; by some faes, certain, more &quot;serious&quot; ways of understanding might be anathema (like bureaucratic magick)<br /> <br /> (and Mages might take more time reading the cards, small dicepools and all that <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-04T18:07:39-08:00","id":800856,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#141823\">Mages are limited by their paradigm. Changelings are limited by their imagination and personal preference. A technomage isn't likely to write &quot;speak friend and enter&quot; in Sindarin on a wall to create a door because it's not likely her paradigm incorporates Tolkeinisms; she's more likely to write out code in a programming language to &quot;change things&quot; and hack a door into place. A changeling can write Sindarin, knock three times and mime turning a knob, click her heels and say &quot;there's no place like inside&quot;, draw the outline of a door with chalk, attempt to Disapparate, stick a key in a hole in the mortar and wait for moonlight to fall on it, anything that suits her tastes.<br /> <br /> Another example using Tolkein: an ascetic mage isn't going to burst out with Galadriel's &quot;treacherous as the sea&quot; speech to help him magically cow an opponent... but a changeling, any changeling, could find it useful as a Bunk for a couple of Arts.</span></span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Luka Carroll</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer &amp; Developer<br /> <i>Working On: </i>C20 Player's Guide, Lunars<br /> <i>Worked On: </i>V20 TMR, Demon STG, C20, Book of Freeholds, Conquering Heroes, Building A Legend, Dragon-Blooded, The Realm","edited":{"userid":3785,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3785-luka-c","user":"Luka C","date":".  Correcting tiny font. 01-04-2016, 09:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3785-luka-c","name":"Luka C","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3785_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"175"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-04T18:41:39-08:00","id":800868,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maggie C</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/798189-the-problem-with-bunks?p=800856#post800856\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#141823\">Mages are limited by their paradigm. Changelings are limited by their imagination and personal preference. A technomage isn't likely to write &amp;quot;speak friend and enter&amp;quot; in Sindarin on a wall to create a door because it's not likely her paradigm incorporates Tolkeinisms; she's more likely to write out code in a programming language to &amp;quot;change things&amp;quot; and hack a door into place. A changeling can write Sindarin, knock three times and mime turning a knob, click her heels and say &amp;quot;there's no place like inside&amp;quot;, draw the outline of a door with chalk, attempt to Disapparate, stick a key in a hole in the mortar and wait for moonlight to fall on it, anything that suits her tastes.</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>Or the pooka could simply shout MOO! for the hell of it, because why not? Maybe she's a contrarian and rejects your need for thematic relationships, or maybe she's just thinking of that delicious glass of chocolate milk she had before being chased off. Bunks don't have to have anything to do with the magic being cast <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Charlie Cantrell</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer <hr />Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition, Conquering Heroes, Book of Freeholds, Guide to the Night, C20 Players Guide","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","name":"PookaKnight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"690"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-04T19:06:37-08:00","id":800874,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PookaKnight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/798189-the-problem-with-bunks?p=800868#post800868\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Or the pooka could simply shout MOO! for the hell of it, because why not? Maybe she's a contrarian and rejects your need for thematic relationships, or maybe she's just thinking of that delicious glass of chocolate milk she had before being chased off. Bunks don't have to have anything to do with the magic being cast <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>You see, RAW or not, I'd reward Bunks that do have some connection to the magic being performed. The Dreaming is full of narrative threads and subconscious meanings. In my opinion, there should at least be a dream-logic to Bunks. Random, unrelated acts become an easy way to get a difficulty reduction. <br /> <br /> 'Wanna use Sovereign on that dragon? Well just do something silly and get on with it.'","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-04T19:17:02-08:00","id":800877,"title":"","content":"It depends on the character. Sure, a sidhe noble is probably going to stick to certain themes, but it would diminish the game greatly if there wasn't room for random, sometimes off the wall improv.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Charlie Cantrell</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer <hr />Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition, Conquering Heroes, Book of Freeholds, Guide to the Night, C20 Players Guide","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","name":"PookaKnight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"690"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-04T22:09:24-08:00","id":801031,"title":"","content":"When an order of Hermes member looks into the future by cutting open a sheep and reading its entrails he does so in accordance with exacting principles handed down from ancient days to gain the secret knowledge of the gods. When a Red cap bites a sheep in half and reads the entrails he does so because its fucking scary to people in modern times, Meat is delicious and he is a creature of primal hunger and fear.<br /> <br /> Mages do something because they belief. Changeling do something because they think its cool.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-05T02:18:07-08:00","id":801230,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PookaKnight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/798189-the-problem-with-bunks?p=800877#post800877\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It depends on the character. Sure, a sidhe noble is probably going to stick to certain themes, but it would diminish the game greatly if there wasn't room for random, sometimes off the wall improv.</div> </div> </div> </div>Improv is different to just doing something unrelated, though. You can improvise a Bunk that has resonance with the thing you want to achieve. That requires *more* creativity and *greater* wits than just saying, 'Oh, I'll just moon that passing car and hope for the best.' <br /> <br /> Of course, mooning a car might suit the cantrip being cast, but doing it for Omen, say, seems irrelevant. If a changeling still gets a difficulty reduction for doing something irrelevant just because it's silly, then you're not actually rewarding creativity but silliness. And it cheapens the system. People perform Bunks just to get a difficulty modifier, even though the Bunk itself doesn't require any real effort.<br /> <br /> People always complain that Changeling is silly, and its fans always defend it against that charge. But we can't if the game actively says, 'We'll make the game easier for you if you're randomly silly all the time.'","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-05T05:23:15-08:00","id":801292,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/798189-the-problem-with-bunks?p=801230#post801230\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If a changeling still gets a difficulty reduction for doing something irrelevant just because it's silly, then you're not actually rewarding creativity but silliness. And it cheapens the system.</div> </div> </div> </div>Does it? To me it seems like it's reinforcing the themes of the game - taking a piss on expectations and giving the finger to banality. Again, it wouldn't work for all characters, but it seems right at home with the punk rock pooka who loathes conformity in all its forms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Charlie Cantrell</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer <hr />Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition, Conquering Heroes, Book of Freeholds, Guide to the Night, C20 Players Guide","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","name":"PookaKnight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"690"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-05T05:32:02-08:00","id":801297,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PookaKnight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/798189-the-problem-with-bunks?p=800868#post800868\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Or the pooka could simply shout MOO! for the hell of it, because why not? Maybe she's a contrarian and rejects your need for thematic relationships, or maybe she's just thinking of that delicious glass of chocolate milk she had before being chased off. Bunks don't have to have anything to do with the magic being cast <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>That's all covered under &quot;whatever suits her tastes&quot;. :P MY personal tastes are thematic, so there. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You see, RAW or not, I'd reward Bunks that do have some connection to the magic being performed. The Dreaming is full of narrative threads and subconscious meanings. In my opinion, there should at least be a dream-logic to Bunks. Random, unrelated acts become an easy way to get a difficulty reduction. </div> </div> </div>Depends on how the character spins it, to me. A pooka randomly shouting MOO as a Bunk for Portal Passage might not get a pass in a game I'm running, but a pooka shouting MOO to Portal Passage herself access to the secret cow level and, incidentally, to the other side of the wall, would.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Luka Carroll</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer &amp; Developer<br /> <i>Working On: </i>C20 Player's Guide, Lunars<br /> <i>Worked On: </i>V20 TMR, Demon STG, C20, Book of Freeholds, Conquering Heroes, Building A Legend, Dragon-Blooded, The Realm","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3785-luka-c","name":"Luka C","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3785_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"175"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-05T06:02:17-08:00","id":801311,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maggie C</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/798189-the-problem-with-bunks?p=801297#post801297\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Depends on how the character spins it, to me. A pooka randomly shouting MOO as a Bunk for Portal Passage might not get a pass in a game I'm running, but a pooka shouting MOO to Portal Passage herself access to the secret cow level and, incidentally, to the other side of the wall, would.</div> </div> </div> </div>That poor cow pooka. He just wants to sing an epic ballad about breaking through impossible barriers in the language of his people.... MOO! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/798189-the-problem-with-bunks?p=801230#post801230\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> People always complain that Changeling is silly</div> </div> </div> </div>Apologies ahead of time, but I just can't resist!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Lego Movie</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes, this is real music<br /> Dark, brooding<br /> Important, groundbreaking<br /> Check out the lyrics<br /> <br /> Darkness<br /> No parents<br /> Continued darkness<br /> More darkness, get it?<br /> The opposite of light<br /> Black hole<br /> Curtains drawn<br /> In the basement<br /> Middle of the night<br /> Blacked-out windows<br /> Other places that are dark<br /> Black suit<br /> Black coffee<br /> You get it, that's just the first verse<br /> <br /> Darkness<br /> No parents<br /> Super rich<br /> Kinda makes it better</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Charlie Cantrell</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer <hr />Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition, Conquering Heroes, Book of Freeholds, Guide to the Night, C20 Players Guide","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","name":"PookaKnight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"690"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-05T06:12:49-08:00","id":801316,"title":"","content":"So the primary difference between a list of example Bunks for particular effects, and a list of example Practices for particular effects, would be that a Changeling could perform any of them as his whim and situation demanded, while the Mage would have to have every Practice extend from the same causal theme.<br /> <br /> Changelings would, therefore, to the uninitiated, look like far more random spellcasters than Mages, as the Mage will act within a particular paradigm with particular foci and implements directed in a particular way, while the Changeling could mix a potion one morning and, that afternoon, perform a martial arts kata. A Mage, meanwhile, would stick to potions and other &quot;scientific&quot; media, or would always be focused on the chi-flow.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/827-segev","name":"Segev","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1001"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-05T06:35:05-08:00","id":801338,"title":"","content":"Yeah, mages work magic because they have a model of reality in their head that they believe actually works. They believe in it so much that reality actually behaves that way in their presence. A techno-mage might believe in some sort of master computer code that underlies all reality. For him, he <b>needs</b> to rewrite the code in order to produce his desired effect. Drawing pentagrams, singing ballads, shouting MOO - those sorts of things would never work for him because his version of reality doesn't support them.<br /> <br /> Changelings use glamour to essentially break reality. They're creatures of dream imposing their chaos on the mundane. Their bunks are a little act of creativity that disrupts the mundane enough to let their glamour through. Different changelings have different creative bents and would be more likely to do one sort of thing over another, but anything that would work for one changeling would be able to work for any other changeling even if a pooka might not want to take the same approach as a sidhe (or vice versa). Bigger, more attention grabbing, more complicated, or more risky is better and makes it easier to impose glamour on the mundane. If a changeling's in a pinch, though, and needs her magic to happen <b>RIGHT NOW</b>, a gesture or a shout is enough to make it possible if not easy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Charlie Cantrell</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer <hr />Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition, Conquering Heroes, Book of Freeholds, Guide to the Night, C20 Players Guide","edited":{"userid":648,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","user":"PookaKnight","date":". 01-05-2016, 09:37 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","name":"PookaKnight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"690"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-06T02:37:10-08:00","id":801895,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maggie C</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/798189-the-problem-with-bunks?p=801297#post801297\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's all covered under &amp;quot;whatever suits her tastes&amp;quot;. :P MY personal tastes are thematic, so there. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Depends on how the character spins it, to me. A pooka randomly shouting MOO as a Bunk for Portal Passage might not get a pass in a game I'm running, but a pooka shouting MOO to Portal Passage herself access to the secret cow level and, incidentally, to the other side of the wall, would.</div> </div> </div> </div>This would be my preference. If she's going to the secret cow level, then screaming 'Moo!' might be enough for a level one Bunk (although it still seems too easy, because where's the real risk in going 'Moo'?).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}